{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Dan, a lion's whelp.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he likened him in valor to a lion's whelp, as he springs from Bashan." "<b>And by way</b> of the Kabbalah, Dan is called corresponding to the attribute of Judgment, for so Rachel said concerning him (Genesis 30:6): ״דנני אלהים״, and Moses likened him in his blessing to a lion's whelp corresponding to the attribute of Judgment above, where there is the form of a lion's whelp, and this is clear."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:16.415406804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}